messages:
maria: FYI — staging deploy failed after terraform change that added an ExternalSecret for svc-config. helm render error: template: svc/templates/deployment.yaml:45:26: executing "svc/templates/deployment.yaml" at <.Values.configSecret.name>: nil pointer
ajay: ugh, repro. CI logs show: 'template: ... at <.Values.configSecret.name>: nil pointer evaluating interface {}.name' — chart assumes configSecret exists\kevin: did terraform change the secret name or the annotation? I only saw a flag flip to create ExternalSecret resource instead of a plain Secret\maria: terraform switched module to create k8s_external_secret (external-secrets) when enable_external_secrets = true, so no plain Secret resource is created. chart still expects .Values.configSecret.name when rendering envFrom\sophie: quick question — are we trying to consume ExternalSecret directly via envFrom, or should the ExternalSecret controller create the plain Secret and the chart consume that?\maria: external-secrets controller should sync to a plain Secret, but timing/race in staging pipeline means helm template runs before the controller has materialized the Secret, and our chart code dereferences .Values.configSecret which is sometimes omitted in values.yaml for non-sensitive envs\ajay: simplest fix: guard the template so it doesn't access .Values.configSecret.name when configSecret is null. e.g.:
```
{{- if .Values.configSecret }}
  envFrom:
    - secretRef:
        name: {{ .Values.configSecret.name | quote }}
{{- end }}
```
That avoids nil pointer at render time\kevin: also consider supporting an override via --set to avoid having to add configSecret to every values file. e.g. default to empty map in values.yaml: `configSecret: {}` so template sees map not nil\sophie: if we want to be strict, use `required` to fail faster when chart expects secret always. but in this case we want optional, so guard is right\maria: my immediate concern is helm template step in our pipeline (we run `helm template` before apply) — it still fails if template tries to access `.name` on nil. adding the guard is minimal patch\ajay: another pattern: use `hasKey` or `and` to safely check nested key. Helm tpl can't do hasKey on non-map. If we set default: `{{- $cs := default dict .Values.configSecret }}{{- if $cs.name }}` then safe\kevin: example patch suggestion:
```
{{- $cs := default (dict) .Values.configSecret }}
{{- if $cs.name }}
envFrom:
  - secretRef:
      name: {{ $cs.name | quote }}
{{- end }}
```
This handles empty/missing configSecret and still allows explicit name\maria: perfect. I'll open a tiny chart patch. also adding one-line note in README about external-secrets controller needing to sync before deploy in CI (or we can skip helm template stage)\sophie: for terraform side: could we add an annotation on ExternalSecret so our pipeline can wait for the Secret to appear? e.g., set `meta.terraform.sync-wait: "true"` then pipeline looks for created Secret name and waits up to Xs\kevin: or add a small k8s resource check step in CI that waits for secret `kubectl get secret $NAME --namespace $NS --ignore-not-found=true` loop — cheap and explicit\infra-bot: deploy-blocked: staging helm-template failed for svc (job id: 5623). tagging @oncall for visibility :warning:\maria: created PR https://git.company/repo/pulls/418 with the guard and a default in values.yaml. please review when you have 5m. I added a short note in the pipeline run to skip template check if `skip_template_check=true` (opt-in for now)\ajay: reviewing now — will also add a comment to suggest a small integration test that runs controller in-kind for ExternalSecret sync timing\kevin: lgtm for the template guard. can merge once infra-team ok with README note\sophie: I'll follow up with terraform owners to evaluate adding a module output for the expected Secret name so chart values can be rendered consistently\maria: thanks all. merging the patch after one more approval. tagging for final review: @ajay @kevin :thumbsup:
